      "name": "Water funnel",
      "//": "One row of alternatives: any rain funnel starts the station. produces.funnels lists what may stand here. Yield is physical: rainMmPerDay (a temperate north-east average, about 1100 mm a year) x the funnel's mouth (radiusMm, the source's funnel_radius) x efficiency (Prologue: how much of what lands reaches the vessel - smooth rigid mouths lose little, stitched hide and bark seep and sag). lifeDays is Prologue too: how long one lasts out in the weather before it is past use. Water runs into the vessels set under the funnels first; baseCharges is the station's own small catch that fills after them.",
