  "//portableStations": "A station that is really a thing: a save that has one built gets the item back on the camp's ground (Home.migratePortableStations). A mattress is dropped and slept on (rules.json sleepQuality), never built.",
  "renamedStations": {
    "grass_tent": "simple_hut"
  },
  "//renamedStations": "Old station ids and what they are now: a save's built station, site or packed bundle is renamed when it loads.",
  "//shelters": "Five shelters, each replacing the one before (upgradesFrom: that one must stand on the camp and is taken down into the new one, its materials counted as part of it). effects.windShelter keeps the wind off (0..1), effects.insulation holds a fire's heat indoors (0..1; game-data/warmth.json), rainCover keeps the rain off, shelterLevel orders them. The first, a simple wooden hut, is what the ground of a field or a wood gives in an hour or two; building it where there is no camp makes the camp there. Every build is worked on as a site (camp.json siteMinutes 0): the materials go in at the start and the work is kept between sittings, to be resumed or abandoned (materials back)."
}
